> So what are the benifits of tinning?

Some have already been mentioned...
- Get the intrinsics without stuffing your stomach (especially helpful with
   giants for strength and dragons for their intrinsics).
- Being of low weight you can carry some spare tins to refresh instrinstics
   if you happen to lose them (e.g. floating eyes).
- If you need to be certain to obtain some non-guaranteed effect you may
   want to collect some tins before you start eating them (one application
   is getting teleport control from tengu meat).
- Geting the intrinsic without getting food-posoning from tinned, formerly
   rotten meat (e.g. giant zombies).
- Prevent some dead monsters to revive (trolls).
